{"In `deleteScheduledEmailReminder`, the `immediateDelete` branch posts the SendGrid cancel but never deletes or flags the corresponding `workflowReminder` row, which can leave orphan reminders in the DB for cases like deleted workflows and rescheduled bookings": 0.9449533820152283, "The cancellation loop in `scheduleEmailReminders` (over `remindersToCancel`) awaits each SendGrid request sequentially inside a `for` loop; if many reminders are due this could be slow, consider using `Promise.all` with per-reminder try/catch or small batches to parallelize these calls": 0.3091161549091339, "The new `deleteScheduledSMSReminder` always deletes the `workflowReminder` row (even when `referenceId` is null), while email reminders are now soft-cancelled via a `cancelled` flag and cleaned up by the cron; inconsistent behavior between SMS and email paths may cause issues for later introspection": 0.5432076454162598}